  :from .to-integrate/methodology-seeds-dialog-quotes.md#11:13

  |title You are not good at understanding where the high-signal original data is

  |quote
    you are not good at understanding where the high-signal original data is.

  |occasion
    Sent while the agent, having been told to restore his verbatim text, was
    replacing its polished version with the original — still substituting, in the
    other direction.

  |about
    The least-processed record is the thing to preserve, and an agent will reliably
    misjudge which artifact that is.

  |should-come-to-mind-when
    - You are about to replace someone else's words with your rendering of them.
    - You are deciding which of two versions to keep.
    - You are about to improve something that was already correct.

  |see
    #ver-manufacture-originals
